 {
  "coord": "261:17",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "hedge",
  "note": "Source says a healthy man usually thinks of many things; \"usually\" was dropped.",
  "replacement": "His mind was not in a normal state. A healthy man usually thinks of, feels and remembers countless things at once. Yet he has the power and the will to pick one train of thoughts or events and fix his whole attention on it. A healthy man can tear himself away from his deepest reflections to say a polite word to someone who comes in, and then go back to his own thoughts. In that respect Prince Andrew's mind was not normal. All its powers were more active and clearer than ever, but they worked apart from his will. The most varied thoughts and images filled his mind at the same time. At moments his brain suddenly worked with a vigor, clarity and depth it had never reached when he was well. Then, in the middle of that work, it would veer off to some unexpected idea, and he had no strength to turn it back."
 },
